# Pachelbel, Canon in D for three violins and continuo: the opening, from the oldest
# surviving source, a manuscript score copied ca. 1838-42 (Staatsbibliothek zu Berlin,
# Mus.ms. 16481/8), not from a printed edition. The piece was first printed in 1919.
# The melody is the first violin, which enters in bar 3; the other two violins follow it
# in canon two bars apart and are not played here. The left hand is the continuo's
# two-bar ground bass, written out once in the manuscript and repeated under every bar.
# This covers the first eight bars, the first violin's quarter-note and eighth-note
# statements; the faster variations that follow are not included.
# The piano versions are generated reductions of these two parts. The chords are our
# reading of the ground bass under the canon; the continuo has no figures here.
title: Canon in D
piece: canon-in-d
added: 2026-10-17
source: public-domain
composer: Johann Pachelbel
composer-died: 1706
first-published: 1919
edition: Manuscript score, ca. 1838-42, Staatsbibliothek zu Berlin, Mus.ms. 16481/8 (IMSLP #346264)
key: D major
meter: 4/4
# The manuscript has no tempo mark; the tempo is ours.
tempo: 64
summary: The opening of Pachelbel's canon: the first violin's line over the eight-note ground bass.
figure: held
medium-figure: held
# The eighth-note bars stay as written in Easy.
easy-keep: 5, 6

[Ground] 1-2
melody: | rw | rw |
chords: | D:1 A:1 Bm:1 F#m:1 | G:1 D:1 G:1 A:1 |
left: | D3q A2 B2 F#2 | G2q D2 G2 A2 |

